Z||000000||DXR_DAD||03-18-2000||10:03 PM||||Back from the show, it was a blast!!  (Fiero Fever)! Thanks go to Big O & Stimpy they put on a great show  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I wish some of you guys could have made it....Al  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, we had lots of sun shine, hum.. about 80' I would say. not back in So.SF yet, still up in Turlock with my brother but I had to have my FORUM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ya know? I will have lots of pics in 2 weeks. Also pics of the DXR Rods?? 68RS Camaro, 72SS Chevelle, SS Monte Carlo, 72 Camaro SS.<P>Well it's about 7:00 Time to hit the hot tub it's been a long day.||||reg||14
Z||000001||mshill||03-19-2000||03:32 AM||||I am really disappointed that I missed it.  The good news is that I had enough time after baseball practice to work on my 86SE (previously known as "Swiss Cheese").  I got the wheels on, clutch bled, linkage adjusted, decklid put on, and washed down.<P>So from the time the first bolt was turned to start the rebuild until it rolled out of the garage, exaclty nine weeks.<P>In this time "Swiss Cheese" got the following: fresh block, rebuilt heads, main/rod/cam bearings, performance cam with new lifters and puchrods, welded/ground exhaust manifolds, ultimate free flow cat (gutted), new clutch, new water pump, all new engine sensors, fresh conduit on wiring harness, all new belts and hoses, poly rear and cradle bushings, fresh engine mounts and fresh brakes all around. And to top it all off a red distributor cap and red wires.<P>The most amazing part is... I did all the work myself (except block/head machining).  Thanks to Haynes and even more so to the forum members.<P>THANKS ALL!!!!!!<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-19-2000||11:04 AM||||Good mshill, I'm glad that some work got done. Did you have a good practice? and I got a new steel clutch pedal from Fieroshop and wanted to know about the shift linkage adjustment?? It just doesn't seem to shift smooth like I have heard some say  after they install the new pedal it shifts smooth as a babies  ?   and just like new. Is the shifter cables hard to replace?<P><BR>Thanks for any help!!||||reg||14
Z||000003||fieroshop||03-19-2000||03:24 PM||||DXR_DAD, the shifter cables are not hard just time comsiming. You have to completly take out the center console and move the ecm ouy of the way.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||03-19-2000||04:17 PM||||i can't wait for you to post pics,yea calif is in bitchin weather mode,glad you had a ball and some one to represent us! all.||||reg||14
Z||000005||batboy||03-19-2000||06:10 PM||||Sometimes it's the select arm bushings getting a little sloppy that causes the crappy shifting. If you have a 4 speed or an Isuzu 5 speed, Rodney Dickman has replacement bushings for $12.00 to 12.50 plus shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||03-19-2000||10:32 PM||||Well, 12 hours after leaving CA, I finally made it home. (I hate America Airlines!!!!) I just wanted to take the opportunity to thank everyone wh came. We had a great turnout with a good variety of cars. From Fieros to Classic Chevies (including the blown alky-fueled tube chassis 56) to some classic pickups, everyone was shined up and had a great time according to all reports.  I hope to post some pics if I can- like the GT with the TV in the center console- VCR and Nintendo included. Pretty wld but kinda sad too. <BR>Anyway, hopefully the rest of our luggage will arrive someday and we can get film developed.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||03-19-2000||11:16 PM||||You go Batboy!!, that dang thing is sloppy! I didn't think to check it, man you saved the day. I have Rodney's Price sheet right here on my desk. I think I will replace the cables anyway.<P>Thanks  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||03-19-2000||11:21 PM||||Stimpy, glad you and the little lady made it home safe. It was nice to talk to ya face to face. My brother and I had a ball, I'm sure he will be in contact with your dad soon.<BR>Next trip hope you can bring your car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD||||reg||6
